window.docContents[164].resolve({"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols--L4-___-Out-of-the-line--Questions-to-ask-the-model-so-far":{"contents":"* Question* Check* What the verdict means\n* Where is body A in this state?* points_vectors_and_distances* positionQ reads the state's com .A point from the conventional origin, and BodyOf π retains the body's nominal pair identity.\n* Can position be added to displacement?* points_vectors_and_distances* No; the Space kind layer refuses the distinct vector roles.\n* Is distance interchangeable with displacement length?* points_vectors_and_distances, distance_is_length* No; their scalar magnitudes are related by a theorem, not kind identity.\n* Whose separation is this?* whose_distance* SeparationOf π retains the pair name erased by the upstream distanceQ.\n* Can the separation change between P states?* whose_distance* Yes; distance is ratio-scale and the difference magnitude is the later distance minus the earlier one, computed from each state's centres.\n* Can Q's distance be mixed with P's?* whose_distance* No; distinct pair identities yield distinct separation bearers.\n* Which frame law applies to a displacement?* bare_frames, kinded_frames* Bare F.Vector accepts all three; KVector allows geometric transport, proves observer independence, and refuses the boost law.\n* Where does the observer's velocity live?* observer_motion* On the cart frame context, and not as a summand of the pair displacement.\n* What does the adoption ladder contribute?* adoption_ladder* Stage 3 curates operators; Stage 4 audits the Space boundary and API map.\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009Onboarding: Human Context Protocols\u0009L4 — Out of the line","header":"5.5.9. Questions to ask the model so far","id":"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols--L4-___-Out-of-the-line--Questions-to-ask-the-model-so-far"},"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols--L4-___-Out-of-the-line--Synopsis":{"contents":"\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009Onboarding: Human Context Protocols\u0009L4 — Out of the line","header":"5.5.1. Synopsis","id":"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols--L4-___-Out-of-the-line--Synopsis"},"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Write-Once___-Correctly--The-five-steps--Step-3-___-Build-kind-differentiated-quantities_SEMI_-gate-the-arithmetic":{"contents":"Now write the model's data and forward maps as records of typed quantities, and let the\ninteraction algebra gate the arithmetic: a product is formed only where the\nkinds sanction it (KMul for products, KDiv for quotients), so a wrong\npairing is a compile error, not a wrong number. Same-kind addition is the gate on +; products and\nquotients change kind by the algebra. Authored over an abstract carrier α, the whole record\nre-represents at the proof carrier (ℝ), the rounding spec (binary32), and the executable (Float)\nby one map, preserving every kind.The example's MiniMironovCoeffs α is the pattern: each Mironov-2009 fit constant is a field of its\nown kind — a dry refractive index ndA0 : Quantity refractiveIndexKind α, a relaxation time\ntaub0 : Quantity relaxTimeKind α, a conductivity sigbF0 : Quantity conductivityKind α — so the\nelaborator refuses to pass a relaxation time where a conductivity is expected, even though all three\nerase to the same carrier. Its MiniMironovCoeffs.map re-represents the whole table at any carrier\n(the constants moved from Int to executable Float by one map), each constant keeping its kind.\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009Write Once, Correctly\u0009The five steps","header":"18.1.3. Step 3 — Build kind-differentiated quantities; gate the arithmetic","id":"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Write-Once___-Correctly--The-five-steps--Step-3-___-Build-kind-differentiated-quantities_SEMI_-gate-the-arithmetic"}});